cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these models, please cite the version you used."
title: "tujia-asr: released acoustic models for syllable-level Tujia speech recognition"
abstract: >-
  Two syllable-level CTC acoustic models for Tujia (Northern dialect), both built on
  wav2vec2-xlsr-53-espeak with a BiLSTM CTC head: v0.1 emits 264 toneless syllable
  shapes, v0.2 emits 708 toned syllables with tone marks. Code is MIT-licensed; weights
  and the fine-tuned encoder are released for research use only, and the training
  corpus is not distributed.
authors:
  - name: "ibaibing"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibaibing/tujia-asr"
keywords:
  - Tujia
  - speech recognition
  - low-resource languages
  - CTC
  - tone
  - wav2vec2
